zainium-installer
=================

The installer of Zainium OS. It puts the system from the live ISO onto a disk.

It has two parts:

    zainium-installer   the graphical installer, run by the live user
    zainium-install     the install engine, run as root through pkexec

The engine can also be used on its own for scripted installs.

What it does
------------

  - erases the chosen disk and makes a GPT with an EFI partition and a root
    partition (ext4 with the verity feature)
  - copies the base from the live image, without the live-only files
  - installs Limine and the kernels on the EFI partition, and adds a UEFI
    boot entry; legacy BIOS boot is set up too
  - creates your user, root password, host name, language, keyboard and
    time zone, written into the base so they survive a userland reset
  - removes the live user, its autologin and the installer itself

The installer erases the whole disk it is given. Installing next to another
system is not supported yet.

A screenshot of the first page is in screenshots/welcome.png.

Building
--------

On Zainium OS:

    make
    make install DESTDIR=<zairoot>

This puts both programs and their desktop entry, icon and polkit policy into
overlayer/zaisys of the live root, and the policy into overlayer/syshub too,
where polkitd reads it.

Tests:

    go test ./internal/...

